VoCat's native Windows data plane uses the following official Go modules:

  golang.zx2c4.com/wintun v0.0.0-20230126152724-0fa3db229ce2
  Source and binary distribution: https://www.wintun.net/
  License: MIT

  golang.zx2c4.com/wireguard/windows v1.0.1
  Project: https://www.wireguard.com/
  License: MIT
  Copyright: Copyright (C) 2018-2026 WireGuard LLC. All Rights Reserved.

VoCat imports the WireGuard Windows winipcfg package for Windows network
interface, address, and route configuration. The full license texts are
included in:

LICENSES/wintun-MIT.txt
LICENSES/wireguard-windows-MIT.txt

The checked-in Windows ready-to-run bundles redistribute the unmodified,
Authenticode-signed Wintun 0.14.1 prebuilt DLL alongside VoCat, which uses only
the documented Wintun API. The accompanying prebuilt-binary license is retained
as dist/windows-*/WINTUN-LICENSE.txt. Operators using other builds obtain the
official, architecture-matched DLL separately under those license terms.

Material modifications made by the Windows fork are described in:
MODIFICATIONS.md
